      "writtenOn": "2022-11-11T17:14:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are there actually any instances where CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT is set to a different value from CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT?\n\nIf not, I think a boolean symbol would be clearer that simply applies the \nCONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT setting\n\n```\n    if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_FLOOR))\n      ma \u003d MAX(ma, CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_INPUT_LIMIT);\n```\n\nNaming is hard, suggestions for the boolean name:\nCONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_FLOOR\nCONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_CLAMPED",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2339,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2339,
        "endChar": 45
